# Multilenguaje playground — mandatory (alwaysApply)

## Locales definitivos (ISO)

Toda UI de playground / test bajo `packages/nextjs` **debe** incluir estos 5 idiomas:

| Code | Language | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `en` | English | Default when browser is not `es-*` / `pt-*` |
| `es` | Español (Argentina) | Flag 🇦🇷 (not 🇪🇸). Default when browser is `es-*` |
| `pt-BR` | Português (Brasil) | Default when browser is `pt-*` |
| `zh` | 中文 (Simplified Mandarin) | CJK system font fallbacks |
| `ar` | العربية | **RTL** — set `dir="rtl"` on `html` when active |

Do **not** hardcode playground strings in a single language. Use dictionaries / message catalogs keyed by locale.

## Language switcher

- Visible in the site header.
- **Flags only** (no visible language names in the UI chrome).
- Each option: accessible `aria-label` (and optional `title`) with the language name, e.g. `Español (Argentina)`, `Português (Brasil)`. Locale `es` uses the **Argentina** flag (🇦🇷), never Spain (🇪🇸).
- `data-testid="locale-switcher"` on the control group.
- Keyboard operable, `:focus-visible` with `--sg-accent`, touch targets ≥ 44×44 px (WCAG 2.5.5).
- Persist choice (`localStorage` or cookie). Sensible default: `es` if `es-*`, `pt-BR` if `pt-*`, else `en`.

## Branding vs i18n

- README “Para todos” may stay ES/EN for global builders; the **app** must be i18n.
- Header logo: mascot image only (no personal name wordmark). Product name secondary: **scaffold-arc**.
- Footer/credit: **Powered by [AcademiaQA.com](https://academiaqa.com)** still required in READMEs.

## Fonts

Keep Baloo 2 + DM Sans for Latin. For `zh` / `ar` (and any future CJK/RTL scripts), document system fallbacks in CSS so glyphs render without breaking brand tokens.
